{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PivotalCategory","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedTensorDual","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TwistedQuantumDimension"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.sphericalOfRibbon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.sphericalOfRibbon","kind":"instance","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L141-L149","doc":"**Every ribbon right-rigid category is spherical** (Barrett–Westbury).\n\nThe pivotal structure is `pivotalOfRibbon`; the condition is discharged by\n`qDimTwistedLeftWith_eq`, where the ribbon axiom is used exactly once, on the cap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalLeft_eq_qDimTwistedLeftWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalLeft_eq_qDimTwistedLeftWith","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L106-L133","doc":"**The left pivotal dimension is the twisted braided closure taken the other way.**\n\nThe evaluation form does not reach this one — the pivotor appears whiskered on the *left*, against a\ncoevaluation — which is what `coev_comp_rightDualIso` is for.  After it, the swapped coevaluation\n`η ≫ β⁻¹` appears literally, and braiding naturality moves the inverse twist from one side of it to\nthe other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalRight_eq_qDimTwistedWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalRight_eq_qDimTwistedWith","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L93-L104","doc":"**The right pivotal dimension is the twisted braided closure.**\n\n`pivotalOfRibbon`'s pivotor is `θ_X ≫ drinfeldIso X`, and `drinfeldIso` is by definition the\ncomparison of `X` and `Xᘁᘁ` as right duals of `Xᘁ`; `rightDualIso_hom_evaluation` is exactly the\nstatement that it converts the evaluation of `Xᘁ ⊣ Xᘁᘁ` into the swapped evaluation\n`β ≫ ε`, which is the closure `qDimTwistedWith` uses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory.qDimPivotalLeft_eq_qDimPivotalRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory.qDimPivotalLeft_eq_qDimPivotalRight","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The left and right quantum dimensions of every object agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory.toPivotalCategory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory.toPivotalCategory","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L84-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SphericalCategory","kind":"class","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**A spherical category**: a pivotal category whose two quantum dimensions agree.\n\nThis is a *condition* on a pivotal structure, not extra data, and it does not follow from pivotality\n— see the module docstring.  `sphericalOfRibbon` below derives it from a balancing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalLeft","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L75-L78","doc":"**The left quantum dimension**: the mirror image — open with the coevaluation of `Xᘁ ⊣ Xᘁᘁ`,\ncome back along the pivotor, and close with the evaluation of `X ⊣ Xᘁ`.  No braiding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimPivotalRight","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SphericalCategory.lean#L69-L73","doc":"**The right quantum dimension of an object in a pivotal category**: open the loop with the\ncoevaluation of `X ⊣ Xᘁ`, cross to the double dual with the pivotor, and close with the evaluation\nof `Xᘁ ⊣ Xᘁᘁ`.  No braiding. ","signatureChunk":0}]}